---
import Legal from '../layouts/Legal.astro';
import { brand } from '../config/brand';

/**
 * ── NEEDS LEGAL REVIEW BEFORE LAUNCH ───────────────────────────────────────
 * This is a plain-language starting point describing how the site and the
 * engagements actually work. It is deliberately modest: it makes no sweeping
 * liability disclaimers and claims no protections that have not been drafted
 * by a lawyer, because terms that read authoritative without being reviewed
 * are worse than terms that are obviously a starting point.
 *
 * Have an Indiana attorney review this before the site goes live, and replace
 * the sections that matter to the business — limitation of liability, IP
 * ownership of delivered materials, and payment terms in particular.
 * ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
 */
---

<Legal
  title="Terms"
  eyebrow="Terms"
  updated="21 September 2026"
  description="The terms that apply to this website, and how MISE OPS engagements are agreed. Prices shown are starting points, not offers."
>
  <h2>About these terms</h2>
  <p>
    These terms cover <strong>this website</strong>. They are not the agreement for a piece
    of work — every MISE OPS engagement is agreed in a separate written scope and quote
    that you see and accept before anything starts. Where the two differ, the signed scope
    wins.
  </p>

  <h2>What this site is</h2>
  <p>
    Marketing information about a service. It describes how MISE OPS works and what an
    engagement can include. It is written to be accurate, but it is general information
    rather than advice about your specific restaurant.
  </p>

  <h3>Pricing shown here</h3>
  <p>
    Figures on this site say <strong>“starting around”</strong> and mean it. They are entry
    points for a scoped engagement, not a fixed price list and not an offer capable of
    acceptance. What your restaurant would cost depends on scope, and you will be given
    that in writing before you commit to anything.
  </p>

  <h3>Examples and demonstrations</h3>
  <p>
    Every example on this site uses a fictional demonstration restaurant and is labelled as
    such. Nothing on this site is a customer, a result, a testimonial or a case study. We
    will add real ones when we have permission to.
  </p>

  <h2>The walkthrough</h2>
  <p>
    Requesting an Operations Walkthrough does not commit you to anything and does not cost
    anything. It also does not oblige us to take the work on — if MISE OPS is not the right
    fit for your restaurant, we will say so.
  </p>

  <h2>Using this site</h2>
  <p>
    The text, design, images and code on this site belong to MISE OPS. You are welcome to
    read it, print it and share links to it. Please do not copy it wholesale for a
    competing service.
  </p>
  <p>
    Do not use the form to send abuse, spam, or anything unlawful, and do not attempt to
    disrupt or gain unauthorised access to the site.
  </p>

  <h2>Availability and accuracy</h2>
  <p>
    We keep this site accurate and online, but we cannot promise it is error-free or never
    unavailable. If something here is wrong, tell us and we will fix it.
  </p>

  <h2>Links to other sites</h2>
  <p>
    Where this site links somewhere else, that site is not under our control and these
    terms do not apply to it.
  </p>

  <h2>Governing law</h2>
  <p>
    These terms are governed by the laws of the State of Indiana, United States.
  </p>

  <h2>Changes</h2>
  <p>
    If these terms change, the date at the top changes with them.
  </p>

  <h2>Contact</h2>
  <p>
    <a class="link" href={`mailto:${brand.email}`}>{brand.email}</a>
  </p>
</Legal>
